            "review_text": "DougJ25\nNew York City, New York1287 contributions\n0\nOne of a Kind Setting\nFeb 2019 • Friends\nOur tour of 5 was treated to a private dinner at Tha Om Garden House. The proprietor, Mr Vinh, first welcomes you with an explanation of the house and gardens and his family history. He leaves you to be taken care of by two young Vietnamese women. \n\nYou dine outside in a courtyard in the middle of the house’s five buildings. Open to the sky, it’s a perfect setting to hear frogs and dogs. \n\nThe meal is a prix fixe menu cleverly written on a fan (a souvenir). Highlights included spring rolls, grilled beef cooked on tiles (in front of you) with sticky rice. \n\nOne of a kind experience. \n\nTip: alcohol and water are extra and the restaurant is cash only.\nRead more\nWritten February 15, 2019",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-03",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
