            "review_text": "Holly R\nChapel Hill, North Carolina1010 contributions\n0\nA Special Evening\nJan 2019 • Friends\nOur tour agent arranged for our small group to have dinner here as part of our itinerary in Hue. I was leery about it as I was worried it would feel like an intrusive experience as it was described as \"enjoying a home cooked meal with the family.\" Luckily, it wasn't like having a meal with the family. The owner, and descendent of the Mandarin family who once lived here, is an architect who has lovingly and painstakingly restored this Mandarin home to it's former glory. Half the house was completely destroyed during the Tet Offensive in 1968. The owner speaks charmingly of his obsession in restoring the home as well as what the life of a Mandarin was like 3 generations ago. His English is excellent. After an introduction to his home, you are led to the dining area. The menu is beautifully lettered on a handmade fan. There is a choice of red or white wine, which you can purchase by the bottle. \nThe gardens are lovely and romantic. The house is set back quite far from the street and you walk down a dirt lane to reach the entrance. When you leave, the young women take you by lantern light back down the alley, which is now quite dark. The feeling is of being served in an historic home, rather than sitting down with a family. Which I was grateful for. The owner's wife does the cooking, but we did not meet her. Two lovely young women helped serve the meal. The food was not, in my opinion, the best we had in Vietnam. But the food wasn't really the point. You were there for the atmosphere and as a guest. And I am sure the food varies on a nightly basis. I don't know how you arrange to eat here, or even how much it costs, as this was part of our tour. But everyone in our group really enjoyed the experience and it was done with characteristic Vietnamese grace.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten February 2, 2019",
            "rating": 5.0,
