            "review_title": "Review at Tha Om Garden House",
            "review_text": "JEBrooklyn\nNew York City, New York22 contributions\n2\nRomantic and Unique\nJul 2018 • Couples\nThis was a very unique experience. Other reviews accurately describe the dinner—about 8 courses served to us by a solicitous attendant in a private courtyard—in a lovingly restored Mandarin house. It’s like stepping back into time. The owner who greets you and gives a short tour is gracious, elegant, and also seems to be a bit from a bygone era. You are a long way away from the modern-day bustle of contemporary Vietnam. \n\nWhile the food and service were great—albeit, as others have said, very expensive—the main thing here is the ambience. It’s truly one of the most unique experiences my husband and I have had. Highly recommended for anyone with an appreciation of history.\nRead more\nWritten July 13, 2018",
