            "review_title": "Review at Tha Om Garden House",
            "review_text": "RAFYKO\nLJUBLJANA75 contributions\n1\nmandarin legacy\nMar 2017\nTha Om garden house is quite a special place in Hue. It is the former villa of the ministry of justice at the court of the emperor Khai Dinh who reigned during nine years (1916-1925) and is owned by his grandson Mr. Pham Ba Vinh who is achitect by profession and who was born after his grandfather death. The villa itself is restored magnificently surrounded by four ponds with several terraces where the eight course dinner is served. Mr. Pham Ba Vinh is talkative person but he knows more about feng shu than about his grandfather and the dinner is slightly overpriced - 80,00 USD without soft drinks or wine. Nevertheless there are two most memorable moments - the presentation of the fan with hand written menu of the dinner on it as a gift of the host to the guest and the farewell from the villa walking through the garden preceeded by a lady in waiting holding a magnificent lantern from the bygone era which can be seen only in some historical movies.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten April 7, 2017",
